## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to reason about data deletion in log-based, multi-tenant systems; covers tombstone propagation, privacy guarantees, auditability, and verification under failure conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Tombstone semantics, cross-topic propagation, and per-tenant isolation
- Idempotence, retention versus deletion semantics
- Audit trails and verification under failure conditions
- Handling cross-topic joins while preserving deletion markers
- Compression-aware deletion propagation

## Code Example
```javascript
function createTombstone(tenantId, key, deletionTimestamp) {
  return {
    tenantId,
    key,
    deletionTimestamp,
    isTombstone: true
  };
}

function propagateTombstone(tombstone, pipeline) {
  pipeline.forEach(stage => {
    stage.emit(tombstone);
    stage.compress(); // Preserve tombstone through compression
  });
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to integrate external data stores with Kafka Streams while maintaining fault tolerance and delivery guarantees.

## Key Concepts
- TTL caches
- Side-input streams and cache invalidation
- MongoDB outage handling with exponential backoff strategy
- Offset management and at-least-once delivery guarantees
- Canary testing

## Code Example
```java
class EnrichmentSink {
  Map<String, VehicleRef> cache;

  void onEvent(VehicleEvent e) {
    VehicleRef ref = cache.get(e.vehicleId);
    if (ref == null) {
      ref = fetchFromMongoDB(e.vehicleId);
      cache.put(e.vehicleId, ref);
    }
    emit(enrich(e, ref));
  }

  void onRefUpdate(VehicleRef r) {
    cache.invalidate(r.vehicleId);
  }
}
```
